6864               /ON ANY ERROR, WE COME HERE.  IF THE USER THAT CAUSED THE ERROR
6865               /WAS NOT WAITING FOR THE DECTAPE, WE CLEAR HIS INPUT WAIT BIT, SET
6866               /HIS ERROR BIT, AND LEAVE.  IF HIS DECTAPE WAIT BIT IS ON, HE
6867               /EITHER ALREADY HAS THE DECTAPE , OR HE IS WAITING ON THE QUEUE.
6868               /SINCE HE IS WAITING, THE ERROR COULD ONLY HAVE BEEN CAUSED
6869               /BY AN INTERRUPT - ^C, KEYBOARD BUFFER FULL, OR THE LIKE.  IF HE
6870               /IS AT THE TOP OF THE QUEUE, WE ASSUME HE HAS THE DECTAPE, AND
6871               /DON'T BOTHER HIM HERE EXCEPT FOR HIS INPUT WAIT AND ERROR BITS.
6872               /IF HOWEVER, HE WAS PUT TO SLEEP BY DTGRAB, AND IS STILL WAITING
6873               /TO GET AT THE DECTAPE ROUTINE, IT WOULD BE A SHAME TO MAKE HIM
6874               /WAIT FOR ALL THE USERS AHEAD OF HIM IN THE QUEUE (WHICH COULD BE
6875               /AS MANY AS SEVEN SEEKS FROM ONE END OF THE TAPE TO THE OTHER)
6876               /JUST TO FIND OUT THAT HE WAS TRYING TO CANCEL THE OPERATION ANYWAY.
6877               /IN THAT CASE, WE TURN OFF HIS DECTAPE WAIT BIT AND SQUISH HIM OUT
6878               /OF THE DECTAPE QUEUE.  UNFORTUNATELY DTFREE WILL ONLY REMOVE HIM
6879               /IF HE IS ALREADY AT THE TOP OF THE QUEUE.
